# Allow-list build context: only what the images need is sent to Docker.
# Everything else is excluded, including in particular:
#   .git .venv .env caches (__pycache__, .pytest_cache, .mypy_cache, .ruff_cache)
#   dist/ build/ mlruns/ mlartifacts/ mlflow.db optuna.db outputs/ models/
#   postgres-data/ garage-data/ minio-data/
#   data/raw/ and data/processed/: the ~291 MB Azure trace is never sent to Docker;
#   mount ./data/raw at runtime instead.
*

!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src/
!docker/

# Never ship bytecode or caches that live inside allowed directories.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.DS_Store
